            <ArticleTitle>Studies on the antioxidant and analgesic activities of Aztec marigold (Tagetes erecta) flowers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1692-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ptr.2550</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Commercially available Aztec marigold (Tagetes erecta) flower extract (Af.Cr) was evaluated for the in vitro antioxidant activity and in vivo analgesic effect on acetic-acid-induced abdominal writhing. The results revealed the presence of pronounced antioxidant potential in Aztec marigold flowers and a dose-dependent (100 and 300 mg/kg) analgesic effect. The antioxidant and analgesic activities obtained seem to be in good accordance with the medicinal uses of Aztec marigold as an anti-inflammatory and analgesic.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>(c) 2008 John Wiley &amp; Sons, Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
